# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in ONE of the two keys — or neither.
#
# NOTHING here is required. With no key at all the app runs completely: the five
# effects, the chain, the export, the whole UI. Only the AI panels (Art Dir,
# Agent, Optimizer) fall back to their built-in offline answers, which are real
# usable presets — just not tailored to what you are actually doing.
#
# The server prints which provider it picked on every boot. Read that line.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Option 1 (recommended): Groq ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free, no credit card. Sign up at https://console.groq.com with an email or a
# Google/GitHub account and create a key. The default model is Llama 3.3 70B —
# much better at returning strict JSON than a small flash model, which is what
# the Optimizer and the Agent actually need. Free-tier limits are roughly
# 30 requests/minute and 1000/day: far more than these panels will ever use.
GROQ_API_KEY=""

# Override the models only if Groq rejects the defaults. The server logs the
# reason as `[ai:groq] groq 400: ...` — read it before guessing.
# GROQ_MODEL_FAST="llama-3.3-70b-versatile"
# GROQ_MODEL_PRO="llama-3.3-70b-versatile"

# ── Option 2: Gemini ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Also free, from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — no credit card either.
# Used only when GROQ_API_KEY is empty.
GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# If every Gemini call falls back instantly, the model id is the first suspect,
# not the key. Override it here rather than editing the code.
# GEMINI_MODEL_FAST="gemini-2.5-flash"
# GEMINI_MODEL_PRO="gemini-2.5-pro"

# ── Deployment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where this app is hosted. AI Studio injects it at runtime; unused locally.
# APP_URL=""
